Let $z = a + bi$ where $a$ and $b$ are real numbers. Then, $\bar{z} = a - bi$. We have
\begin{align*}
(\bar{z})^{2} + \frac{4}{z^{2}} &= (a - bi)^{2} + \frac{4}{(a + bi)^{2}} \\
&= (a^{2} - b^{2} - 2abi) + \frac{4}{a^{2} + 2abi - b^{2}} \\
&= (a^{2} - b^{2} - 2abi) + \frac{4(a^{2} - 2abi - b^{2})}{(a^{2} + b^{2})^{2}} \\
&= (a^{2} - b^{2} - 2abi) + \frac{4a^{2} - 8abi - 4b^{2}}{(a^{2} + b^{2})^{2}} \\
&= (a^{2} - b^{2}) - 2abi + \frac{4a^{2}}{(a^{2} + b^{2})^{2}} - \frac{8ab}{(a^{2} + b^{2})^{2}}i - \frac{4b^{2}}{(a^{2} + b^{2})^{2}} \\
&= \left( (a^{2} - b^{2}) + \frac{4a^{2}}{(a^{2} + b^{2})^{2}} - \frac{4b^{2}}{(a^{2} + b^{2})^{2}} \right) + \left( -2ab - \frac{8ab}{(a^{2} + b^{2})^{2}} \right)i
\end{align*}
For the real and imaginary parts to be integers, we must have
\begin{align*}
(a^{2} - b^{2}) + \frac{4a^{2}}{(a^{2} + b^{2})^{2}} - \frac{4b^{2}}{(a^{2} + b^{2})^{2}} &= \text{integer} \\
-2ab - \frac{8ab}{(a^{2} + b^{2})^{2}} &= \text{integer}
\end{align*}
Let's analyze the second equation. We have
\begin{align*}
-2ab - \frac{8ab}{(a^{2} + b^{2})^{2}} &= \text{integer} \\
-2ab \left( 1 + \frac{4}{(a^{2} + b^{2})^{2}} \right) &= \text{integer} \\
\Rightarrow\qquad 1 + \frac{4}{(a^{2} + b^{2})^{2}} &= \frac{\text{integer}}{-2ab}
\end{align*}
Since $1 + \frac{4}{(a^{2} + b^{2})^{2}} > 1$, we must have $-2ab < 0$, which implies $ab > 0$. Now, let's analyze the first equation. We have
\begin{align*}
(a^{2} - b^{2}) + \frac{4a^{2}}{(a^{2} + b^{2})^{2}} - \frac{4b^{2}}{(a^{2} + b^{2})^{2}} &= \text{integer} \\
(a^{2} - b^{2}) + \frac{4(a^{2} - b^{2})}{(a^{2} + b^{2})^{2}} &= \text{integer} \\
(a^{2} - b^{2}) \left( 1 + \frac{4}{(a^{2} + b^{2})^{2}} \right) &= \text{integer} \\
\Rightarrow\qquad (a^{2} - b^{2}) \left( \frac{\text{integer}}{-2ab} \right) &= \text{integer} \\
\Rightarrow\qquad \frac{a^{2} - b^{2}}{-2ab} &= \text{integer} \\
\Rightarrow\qquad \frac{a}{b} - \frac{b}{a} &= \text{integer}
\end{align*}
Since $ab > 0$, we have $\frac{a}{b} > 0$ and $\frac{b}{a} > 0$. Let $\frac{a}{b} = x$ and $\frac{b}{a} = \frac{1}{x}$. Then, we have
\begin{align*}
x - \frac{1}{x} &= \text{integer} \\
\Rightarrow\qquad \frac{x^{2} - 1}{x} &= \text{integer}
\end{align*}
This implies $x^{2} - 1$ is an integer multiple of $x$. Since $x > 0$, we have $x \geq 1$. Now, let's try some values of $x$. If $x = 1$, then $a = b$, and we have
\begin{align*}
1 + \frac{4}{(a^{2} + b^{2})^{2}} &= \frac{\text{integer}}{-2ab} \\
1 + \frac{4}{(2a^{2})^{2}} &= \frac{\text{integer}}{-2a^{2}} \\
1 + \frac{1}{a^{4}} &= \frac{\text{integer}}{-2a^{2}} \\
\Rightarrow\qquad \frac{a^{4} + 1}{a^{4}} &= \frac{\text{integer}}{-2a^{2}} \\
\Rightarrow\qquad \frac{a^{4} + 1}{-2a^{2}} &= \text{integer}
\end{align*}
Since $a^{4} + 1 > a^{4}$, we must have $-2a^{2} < 0$, which implies $a^{2} > 0$. Now, we have
\begin{align*}
\frac{a^{4} + 1}{-2a^{2}} &= \text{integer} \\
\Rightarrow\qquad a^{4} + 1 &= -2a^{2} \cdot \text{integer} \\
